<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the hardened runtime, applied to Chora.app and inherited by
  its helper processes.

  Deliberately minimal. Every entitlement here is a hole in the hardened
  runtime, so nothing is listed that the app does not actually need.

  Removed 2026-09-02, after a security review:

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      A legacy requirement from older Electron versions. Modern Electron gets
      what V8 needs from allow-jit alone. Verified: the app packages and signs
      cleanly without it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!-- Required by V8: JavaScript is compiled to executable memory at runtime. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      LOAD-BEARING ONLY BECAUSE THE BUILD SIGNS AD-HOC.

      This weakens the hardened runtime: it lets any dylib — unsigned, or signed
      by anyone at all — be loaded into the Chora process, which is the standard
      macOS code-injection path. Chora has no native modules, so nothing
      legitimate needs it.

      It cannot be removed yet. Library validation matches a loaded library's
      Team ID against the main binary's, and package.json → build.mac.identity
      is "-" (ad-hoc), which produces no Team ID at all. electron-builder warns
      on this directly:

        "ad-hoc signing with hardenedRuntime enabled requires the
         com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation entitlement to
         prevent app launch failures due to library validation."

      Removing it was tried on 2026-09-02 and reverted for that reason.

      DELETE THIS KEY the day the build switches to a Developer ID identity.
      That is the change library validation is designed to pair with, and it is
      the single remaining step to a fully hardened runtime.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
